📄 Group Project: Pampered Pets Risk Assessment Report

As part of Unit 6 of the SRM_PCOM7E module, I collaborated with a development team to produce a comprehensive risk identification report for a fictional SME called Pampered Pets. This report focused on mapping out cybersecurity and operational risks affecting their digital infrastructure, specifically their online booking system, database access, and internal IT policies.

🔍 Key Contents:

A stakeholder-based risk register identifying over 12 core risks

Likelihood vs. Impact matrix (5x5) with colour-coded risk levels

Strategic recommendations using ISO 27005 and NIST guidance

Emphasis on weak password policies, poor access controls, insider threats, and unpatched software

Risk mitigation aligned with confidentiality, integrity, and availability (CIA Triad)

